-- Hand-authored media interview answers for promotion, rivals, social media, success and touring.
WITH tailored(question_text,a,b,c,d) AS (VALUES
('Do you enjoy promotion or just tolerate it?', 'I enjoy getting to explain why the songs matter.', 'Promotion is work, but connecting with listeners makes it worthwhile.', 'I''d rather play than talk, but a good interview can be fun.', 'Ask me after my sixth interview of the day.'),
('Do you know immediately which song should be a single?', 'Sometimes a chorus announces itself right away.', 'We test a few candidates before deciding.', 'Our strangest track might be the biggest single.', 'Usually the band votes against my favourite.'),
('Does a weak single mean the campaign has failed?', 'No; one song doesn''t tell the whole album''s story.', 'We look at engagement and the next release opportunity.', 'A disappointing single can lead to a stronger comeback.', 'Maybe it just means the cover art was cursed.'),
('How closely do you watch first-week numbers?', 'I check them, but the songs matter more than the chart.', 'Our team tracks figures so we can plan the next steps.', 'The numbers tell us whether people are paying attention.', 'I refresh the page more than I''d like to admit.'),
('How do you keep talking about the same record without sounding rehearsed?', 'Every listener hears a different detail worth discussing.', 'I focus on the story behind whichever track comes up.', 'I try to give a real answer instead of repeating press notes.', 'Sometimes I invent a new metaphor just to stay awake.'),
('How much should fans hear before an album comes out?', 'Enough to get excited without losing the surprise.', 'A couple of singles provide a good preview.', 'I''d reveal almost nothing and let the whole record land.', 'I still want to hide one secret track.'),
('How nervous are you before releasing new music?', 'Very; sharing something personal always feels vulnerable.', 'Excitement and nerves usually arrive together.', 'The scarier a release feels, the more I know it matters.', 'I pretend I''m calm while checking every notification.'),
('Would you delay a release if another huge artist announced the same date?', 'I''d keep our date if it''s right for the music.', 'We''d review the schedule, but not panic over competition.', 'I''d welcome the challenge and release anyway.', 'Only if the printer lost all our sleeves.'),
('Would you ever release an album with no warning?', 'Yes, a surprise could make listening feel special.', 'It would depend on whether fans could actually find it.', 'Dropping an album overnight would be thrilling.', 'I''d probably forget to tell the rest of the band.'),
('Would you rather a song grow slowly or explode immediately?', 'Slow growth can build a lasting connection with listeners.', 'Either is fine if people keep coming back to the song.', 'Give me a huge opening moment and let us ride it.', 'I''ll take whichever pays for the next tour.'),
('Do you pay attention to what competing artists release?', 'I listen because good music inspires me.', 'We stay aware without copying anybody''s strategy.', 'If another band raises the bar, we want to clear it.', 'Yes, usually five minutes after they beat us on the chart.'),
('Does rivalry make better music?', 'Healthy competition can push everyone to improve.', 'It helps when the rivalry stays respectful.', 'Nothing fuels a rehearsal like hearing a rival''s killer riff.', 'Sometimes it just fuels bad social posts.'),
('Has another artist ever copied your sound or image?', 'We''ve noticed similarities, but shared influences happen.', 'I''d rather focus on our own new ideas than accuse people.', 'There have been moments that felt suspiciously familiar.', 'If they copy our outfits, they can keep the laundry bill.'),
('Have you ever enjoyed seeing another band fail?', 'I''d rather see musicians succeed than celebrate mistakes.', 'Competition can be intense, but setbacks aren''t a joke.', 'I''ll admit some rival chart drops have made me smirk.', 'Only when their drummer mocked our tempo first.'),
('Is friendly competition in music ever really friendly?', 'It can be when everyone respects the work.', 'Most rivalries mix admiration with ambition.', 'I want to beat our rivals and shake their hands afterwards.', 'Depends on who''s ahead when the chart closes.'),
('Is there an artist you think is wildly overrated?', 'I prefer talking about artists whose work moves me.', 'Popularity means different things to different listeners.', 'Some huge acts have better marketing than songs.', 'I''m not turning this interview into a feud.'),
('Which band would you most like to beat to number one?', 'Whoever''s currently at the top of the chart.', 'A friendly rival would make the moment sweeter.', 'I''d love to knock the biggest act off the summit.', 'Anyone except a band we''re sharing a tour bus with.'),
('Which other band do you see as your biggest competition?', 'The bands pushing our genre forward inspire us most.', 'We compete mainly with the standard of our last release.', 'Any group that can take a crowd from quiet to wild.', 'The band booked in the venue next door.'),
('Would you collaborate with someone you''ve publicly criticised?', 'Yes, if we could be honest and make great music.', 'I''d clear the air first and talk about the project.', 'A great song matters more than an old argument.', 'They can buy the first round at rehearsal.'),
('Would you support a rival band on tour?', 'Absolutely, if the music and audiences fit together.', 'We''d discuss the terms like any other tour.', 'Sharing a bill with rivals could be electric.', 'Only if they agree not to steal our encore.'),
('Do artists reveal too much online now?', 'Some do; everyone deserves a private life.', 'I think artists should set their own boundaries.', 'Posting everything leaves nothing for the songs to reveal.', 'Nobody needs to see every meal on our tour.'),
('Do short-form platforms change the way songs are written?', 'They can affect structure, but we still write full songs.', 'Some artists optimise hooks for clips; we don''t have to.', 'I''d rather make a four-minute anthem than a ten-second trend.', 'If a platform wants a chorus at second one, tough luck.'),
('Do you personally run your social media accounts?', 'I write many posts so they sound like me.', 'We share the workload with our team.', 'Fans can spot it when a page loses its personality.', 'Yes, including the typos.'),
('Does reading comments affect your mood?', 'Sometimes; kind messages can make a rough day better.', 'I limit how long I spend reading reactions.', 'Cruel comments sting even when you know they shouldn''t.', 'One bad comment can ruin five perfect reviews.'),
('Have online arguments ever spilled into real band relationships?', 'Yes; misunderstandings travel quickly from screens to rehearsals.', 'We take sensitive discussions offline and talk properly.', 'A careless post can start a real backstage row.', 'We''ve banned arguments in the group chat after midnight.'),
('Have you ever deleted a post because your team panicked?', 'Yes; sometimes a joke reads badly without context.', 'We''ve reconsidered posts after talking things through.', 'If a message is honest, I won''t delete it just for noise.', 'Apparently my publicist dislikes my late-night humour.'),
('How much should fans know about your private life?', 'Enough to feel connected without crossing personal boundaries.', 'I decide what to share and keep loved ones out of it.', 'Being a fan doesn''t make someone entitled to private details.', 'You can know my pedal settings, not my passwords.'),
('Is going viral actually useful for a serious artist?', 'It helps if the attention leads people to real music.', 'A viral moment is an opportunity, not a career plan.', 'I''d rather have a hundred devoted fans than a million empty views.', 'It pays off if they stay for more than the meme.'),
('Would you quit social media if it didn''t help your career?', 'Yes; I''d rather spend that time making music.', 'I''d scale back before shutting every account.', 'If it stops connecting with fans, it isn''t worth the distraction.', 'Don''t threaten me with an excuse to delete the apps.'),
('Would you rather have one viral hit or a loyal audience built slowly?', 'A loyal audience can carry a band through many albums.', 'I''d welcome a hit if it brings people into our community.', 'I''d choose a lasting following over a week''s explosion.', 'Can the viral hit pay for the slow build?'),
('Are awards meaningful or just industry politics?', 'Recognition feels special when it honours real work.', 'Awards can celebrate music, but they''re not the final measure.', 'Some trophies reveal more about the voters than the songs.', 'I''ll thank the academy if they send a free dinner.'),
('Are you comfortable being recognised in public?', 'Usually; meeting listeners is a lovely surprise.', 'I enjoy brief conversations but protect quiet time.', 'It''s strange having strangers feel they know you.', 'Only when I''m not wearing my worst tracksuit.'),
('Do chart positions still matter to you?', 'They''re exciting, but the connection with fans matters more.', 'Charts help us gauge reach without defining our worth.', 'Of course I want to see our name at number one.', 'Ask me after we drop out of the top ten.'),
('Do you worry that success could disappear quickly?', 'I try to appreciate the moment and keep working.', 'We plan carefully because careers do change.', 'The fear keeps us hungry for the next great record.', 'Every musician checks the ticket sales twice.'),
('Has fame changed the way people treat you?', 'Some people react differently, but close friends keep me grounded.', 'I notice it more in public than in private.', 'It reveals who cared about us before the headlines.', 'Suddenly everyone claims they knew me in school.'),
('How ambitious are you really?', 'I want to keep improving and reach more people.', 'We set big goals without sacrificing what we love.', 'I want our songs heard in every arena on earth.', 'Ask again after I''ve slept for a week.'),
('What would count as ''making it'' for you?', 'Being able to make music full time would be enough.', 'A sustainable career and loyal audience feel like success.', 'Headlining the biggest stages on our own terms.', 'Affording a tour bus with working air conditioning.'),
('What''s the biggest misconception people have about success?', 'That it arrives overnight instead of after years of work.', 'People don''t see how much uncertainty remains.', 'A big crowd doesn''t mean every problem disappears.', 'They think the backstage fridge is always full.'),
('When did you first realise the band was becoming successful?', 'When strangers started singing our lyrics back to us.', 'Selling out a venue we once played half-empty felt special.', 'The first time we heard our name shouted from a huge crowd.', 'When the merch queue was longer than the toilet queue.'),
('Would you trade some fame for more creative freedom?', 'Absolutely; control over our music matters deeply.', 'I''d look for a balance between reach and independence.', 'I''d gladly lose a chart place to make a fearless album.', 'Depends how much fame you''re taking back.'),
('Do you still get nervous before going on stage?', 'Yes, and those nerves remind me it matters.', 'A short warm-up helps me turn anxiety into energy.', 'If I ever stop feeling adrenaline, something''s wrong.', 'My hands shake until the first chord.'),
('Have you ever wanted to cancel a show at the last minute?', 'I''ve had rough days, but the crowd usually lifts me.', 'Safety or illness can make cancellation the right call.', 'Even when things go wrong, I fight to get on stage.', 'Only when I realised I''d forgotten my guitar.'),
('How do you keep a tour from becoming repetitive?', 'We change the set and explore each city.', 'Small routines help while new venues keep things fresh.', 'A different song choice can change the whole night.', 'I keep losing my hotel key to add suspense.'),
('How do you recover after a terrible show?', 'We talk about what happened and focus on the next gig.', 'Rest, rehearsals and honest feedback help.', 'I turn disappointment into a louder performance tomorrow.', 'First I eat something, then I apologise to the drummer.'),
('How much does the crowd change the way you perform?', 'Their energy can make familiar songs feel new.', 'We adapt the pacing and interaction to the room.', 'A wild audience can push us into unplanned encores.', 'If they go quiet, we wonder if the amps died.'),
('What do you miss most when you''re away touring?', 'Time with family and friends at home.', 'Ordinary routines and a familiar bed.', 'Quiet moments where nobody needs another soundcheck.', 'My own pillow, without question.'),
('What is the hardest part of life on tour?', 'Being away from people I love.', 'Keeping healthy through constant travel and late nights.', 'Staying creative when every day looks like a motorway.', 'Finding a working shower after the encore.'),
('What''s the strangest thing that''s happened backstage?', 'Once an unexpected animal wandered into the dressing room.', 'A venue mix-up left us sharing a room with a magician.', 'Someone arrived backstage dressed exactly like our singer.', 'I still can''t explain the missing cake.'),
('Which city has surprised you most on the road?', 'A smaller city gave us one of our loudest crowds.', 'Somewhere we barely knew turned into a favourite stop.', 'The most unexpected cities often deliver unforgettable shows.', 'Whichever city actually had hot food backstage.'),
('Would you rather play ten clubs or one arena?', 'Ten intimate nights let us connect with more people.', 'Both experiences offer something unique.', 'Give me one massive arena and a deafening singalong.', 'Ten clubs, provided nobody loses the van keys.')
)
UPDATE public.interview_questions q SET option_a_text=t.a,option_b_text=t.b,option_c_text=t.c,option_d_text=t.d
FROM tailored t WHERE q.question_text=t.question_text AND q.created_at::date=DATE '2026-09-02';